#
# https://help.github.com/articles/dealing-with-line-endings/
#
# Linux start script should use lf
/gradlew        text eol=lf

# These are Windows script files and should use crlf.
#
# Deliberately -text rather than "text eol=crlf": Dependabot writes wrapper
# updates through the GitHub API, which has no working tree and so never runs
# the eol clean filter. Under "text eol=crlf" it stores the upstream CRLF bytes
# verbatim, and every later checkout then normalises them back to lf, leaving
# gradlew.bat permanently dirty and un-resettable. -text keeps the crlf bytes
# in the object store, so the file matches whoever wrote it.
*.bat           -text

